Package: reCYCLing
Type: Package
Title: Repeat Element Cyclical Evolutionary Simulations in Genomes
Version: 1.0.0
Author: Grey Monroe [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Grey Monroe <greymonroe@gmail.com>
Description: Simulates the evolution of satellite DNA repeat arrays, from
    single tandem arrays to whole multi-chromosome genomes, through local
    (multi-monomer) duplication, long-range duplication, inter-chromosomal
    exchange, governed deletion, and per-base mutation. Computes a catalog of
    summary statistics describing monomer arrays (divergence from consensus,
    identical-pair spatial structure, cross-chromosome sharing, and more) for
    use in approximate Bayesian computation, and provides visualization tools
    for repeat fingerprints, monomer diversity, and array composition.
